// Games you can own. Each is a tiny grid game run by one of core's engines (games::Engine), and
// you come by it one of two ways:
//   a cracked copy  a file `Game(id)` in a board's FILES, signed by a crew: opens with `crack`
//   a boxed copy    by mail order from CPU Shopper's Games section: opens with `splash`
// You can own both copies side by side; each opens with its own intro and has its own label.
// See docs/world.md for the crews and the publisher.
//   id         what boards, the shop and the save call it
//   name       the box's name ("Nibbler"); a cracked copy is the name in capitals with its
//              crew's tag from the crack intro ("NIBBLER [2K4]")
//   blurb      one line for a listing
//   publisher  who sells the boxed copy (a vendor id in shopper.ron)
//   version    its version string, listed in System's About This Deck (default "1.0")
//   engine     the rules it runs: Nibbler (a snake), Blox (falling blocks), Minefield (mines)
//   cols, rows the play field in cells: at least the engine's minimum, at most 78 x 24
//   tick_ms    one tick of the game's clock; the engine counts ticks, never reads a clock
//   crack      the crew's cracktro (an intro in data/intros/ with a board and greetz)
//   splash     the publisher's splash (an intro in data/intros/ with a tagline, no greetz)
//   shop       sold boxed by mail order: Some((price: n)). Leave it out and it's only cracked.
//              None is for sale yet: a game goes in the shop once it opens on the desktop.
[
    (id: "nibbler", name: "Nibbler", blurb: "Steer the snake, eat the dots, and don't bite your own tail.",
     publisher: "papertiger", version: "1.0", engine: Nibbler, cols: 32, rows: 20, tick_ms: 50,
     crack: "nibbler-crack", splash: "nibbler-splash"),
    (id: "blox", name: "Blox", blurb: "Falling blocks: turn them, drop them, clear the lines.",
     publisher: "papertiger", version: "2.0", engine: Blox, cols: 10, rows: 20, tick_ms: 50,
     crack: "blox-crack", splash: "blox-splash"),
    (id: "minefield", name: "Minefield", blurb: "Clear the field square by square. The numbers say how close the mines are.",
     publisher: "papertiger", version: "1.1", engine: Minefield, cols: 16, rows: 16, tick_ms: 100,
     crack: "minefield-crack", splash: "minefield-splash"),
]
